From d5e0ee70836b8360403c9b2ca6e590ea0544917c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:34:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] 027 (TKBO): IsVertexOnLine skips the projection of a
 vertex outside the pole box of the curve

BOPAlgo_PaveFiller::PutPavesOnCurve tests every edge/face vertex of a face pair against every
section curve (IntTools_Context::IsVertexOnLine). After the end-point checks the stock code projects
the vertex on the curve; a section curve of a long B-spline face is a 1001-pole degree-1 B-spline,
so each projection costs O(spans) and the step is O(vertices x curves x spans): 39 % of the section
of the ball screw thread face 153, 26 % of the whole-screw common.

A B-spline or Bezier curve (positive weights) lies in the convex hull of its poles, hence in their
axis-aligned box, over its whole parameter range (the projector's range). If the distance from the
vertex to that box exceeds the tolerance sum (plus a rounding margin 1e-7 + 1e-9 * coordinate scale),
every point the projector can return, and both curve ends, are farther than the tolerance, so the
stock code returns false on every path; the new check returns false before projecting. Other curve
types keep the stock path.

INTTOOLS_027_VERIFY: runs the stock projection too and aborts if a skipped vertex would have been on
the line; INTTOOLS_027_MUTANT_A: skips every projection (negative control).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_Context.cxx        | 141 ++++++++++++++++++
